            SSA requires 35 years. Shorter careers include $0 years.
          </p>
          <select id="years-worked" class="ssb-select">
            <option value="10">10 Years (25 Zero-Earning Years)</option>
            <option value="15">15 Years (20 Zero-Earning Years)</option>
            <option value="20">20 Years (15 Zero-Earning Years)</option>
            <option value="25">25 Years (10 Zero-Earning Years)</option>
            <option value="30">30 Years (5 Zero-Earning Years)</option>
            <option value="35" selected>35+ Years (Full Career Record — Most Common)</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="ssb-field-group">
          <label for="claim-age" class="ssb-label">Planned Claiming Age</label>
          <p class="ssb-help-text">
            Age you plan to start collecting checks (62 to 70).
          </p>
          <select id="claim-age" class="ssb-select">
            <option value="62">Age 62 (Earliest — Permanent 30% Reduction)</option>
            <option value="63">Age 63 (Early Claiming Reduction)</option>
            <option value="64">Age 64 (Early Claiming Reduction)</option>
            <option value="65">Age 65 (Early Claiming Reduction)</option>
            <option value="66">Age 66 (Reduced if FRA is 67)</option>
            <option value="67" selected>Age 67 (Full Retirement Age for workers born 1960+)</option>
            <option value="68">Age 68 (Delayed Retirement Credit +8%)</option>
            <option value="69">Age 69 (Delayed Retirement Credit +16%)</option>
            <option value="70">Age 70 (Maximum Delayed Credit +24%)</option>
